<Hero title="Oxidoc">
<HeroAction label="Get Started" href="/docs/installation" variant="primary" />
<HeroAction label="View on GitHub" href="https://github.com/oxidoc-lab/oxidoc" variant="secondary" />

A documentation engine written in Rust. Zero Node.js. Interactive WebAssembly islands.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="Linux / macOS">
```bash
curl -fsSL https://oxidoc.dev/install.sh | sh
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Windows">
```powershell
irm https://oxidoc.dev/install.ps1 | iex
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

</Hero>

<Section bg="muted">
<FeatureGrid>
<Feature icon="⚡" title="Fast Builds">
Builds thousands of pages in seconds with incremental rebuilds.
</Feature>
<Feature icon="🧩" title="Interactive Islands">
Wasm-powered components like tabs, code blocks, and API playgrounds.
</Feature>
<Feature icon="🔍" title="Search Built-in">
BM25 lexical search out of the box, with optional semantic search for better recall.
</Feature>
<Feature icon="📦" title="Zero Config">
Works out of the box with sensible defaults. Customize when you need to.
</Feature>
</FeatureGrid>
</Section>

